  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ClinRC 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "During a clinical trial visit, a patient mentions that they\u2019ve
    been feeling unusually dizzy and nauseated after starting the trial treatment.\n\n<b>As
    the research coordinator, what should you do in this situation?</b>"
  explanation: Research coordinators help support monitoring and reporting during
    clinical trials by carefully documenting side effects and communicating them
    to the research team. This ensures potential safety concerns are reviewed promptly
    and helps protect participants throughout the study. Sharing this information
    quickly allows the care team to respond if changes or follow-up are needed.
  correctAnswer: Document the side effect and share it with the research team
  incorrectAnswer1: Decide whether the patient should stop or continue the trial
  incorrectAnswer2: Reassure the patient that side effects are expected and no further
    action is needed
  incorrectAnswer3: Change the dose of the trial treatment to prevent further side
    effects
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Clinical
